@@ -0,0 +1,32 @@
+# Design
+
+## Context
+
+`Flask.run` currently obtains host and port defaults by splitting
+`SERVER_NAME` at the first colon. See proposal.md for motivation and the
+development-server-defaults spec for the required behavior.
+
+## Goals / Non-Goals
+
+**Goals:**
+
+- Recognize bracketed IPv6 literals with ports when deriving run defaults.
+- Retain the existing behavior for ordinary host names and port `0`.
+
+**Non-Goals:**
+
+- Changing URL routing or general `SERVER_NAME` handling outside `Flask.run`.
+
+## Decisions
+
+- Treat a value beginning with `[` as a bracketed host, splitting it at the
+  closing bracket and removing the brackets before passing the host to the
+  server. This follows the documented host:port representation and avoids
+  treating an IPv6 address's internal colons as a port separator.
+- Keep the current first-colon split for non-bracketed values, preserving
+  existing hostname behavior.
+
+## Risks / Trade-offs
+
+- [Malformed bracketed values] → Preserve the current fallback behavior unless
+  a valid closing bracket and port separator are present.
