+# Proposal
+
+## Why
+
+`Flask.run` splits `SERVER_NAME` at its first colon, so a bracketed IPv6
+literal is passed to the development server with an invalid host and port.
+
+## What Changes
+
+- Parse bracketed IPv6 `SERVER_NAME` values when selecting default development
+  server host and port.
+- Preserve existing hostname, explicit port, and port-zero behavior.
+
+## Capabilities
+
+### New Capabilities
+
+- `development-server-defaults`: Default host and port selection for
+  `Flask.run` from application configuration.
+
+### Modified Capabilities
+
+- None.
+
+## Impact
+
+- Affects `src/flask/app.py` and the `Flask.run` configuration tests in
+  `tests/test_basic.py`.
